     5	  2  one lifecycle writer: the API is read-only
     6	  3  the fence before every evidence fetch; every lifecycle write guarded on (state, attempt id, version)
     7	  4  eligibility (three conjuncts, k = 6, the attempt's own evidence) and the latch with its preserved presentation
     8	  5  expiry / discard only on complete negative evidence; anything else leaves the attempt open (step 5 is GATED)
     9	  6  after the latch: transient failures retried, incurable ones discarded with a reason, presentation never swapped
    10	  7  atomic end-and-allocate; REFUSED ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED / SIGNING_CLOSED; closed signing never ends a latched or
    11	     signed-and-stamped attempt
    12	  8  the public view
    13	  9  storage lifetime: no age rule on live objects; cleanup tags cleanup-due, then deletes
    14	
    15	Evidence is driven with the stand-in chain and calendar on the fake clock: a stamp stays pending until a block is
    16	mined, the block's time is the clock, and k = 6 needs five more blocks. Races are driven by hooks on the stores, as in
    17	test_confirm_fixes.py; nothing sleeps. Model action names (Start, Fence, Fetch, Send, Commit, Kill, Resend) are used
    18	where a test mirrors one of the model's interleavings."""
    19	import copy
    20	import json
    21	
    22	import pytest
    23	
