   148	8. **Next attempt and refusal.** Ending attempt i and allocating attempt i+1 happen in one guarded write. So a crash
   149	   cannot leave the request between attempts, and a retry cannot run twice. Each ended attempt records
   150	   its own reason: `EXPIRED` (complete negative evidence after B); `DISCARDED` (complete negative evidence before B,
   151	   step 7, or a signer's refusal, `SIGNER_REFUSED:<reason>`: an unsigned, unstamped attempt cannot be timely
   152	   eligible); or `EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE` (step 5, gated). If i = N, the same write ends the request REFUSED with
   153	   `ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED`, listing each attempt's reason. If a new attempt would need signing after the stop, the
   154	   reason is `SIGNING_CLOSED`. A closed signing window never ends a latched or already signed and stamped attempt
   155	   (revision 5, model finding 6).
